From 9df28b1da03892c3a6f98d8074cc2fe78ee2d656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 14:42:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] build: Ask clang for the local-exec TLS model

RTEMS uses static thread-local storage.  clang defaults to initial-exec for
an extern thread-local and emits R_RISCV_TLS_GOT_HI20, which needs a GOT
entry the linker fills in.  That resolves in the base image, but a module
loaded by libdl is relocated at run time with no linker involved, and the
architecture back ends implement only the local-exec TPREL forms -- the
RISC-V one handles R_RISCV_GOT_HI20 but not the TLS variant, so dl11 failed
with "Unsupported relocation type 21".

This is not a clang bug and not RTEMS specific: clang makes the same
conservative choice for riscv32-unknown-elf and riscv32-unknown-linux-gnu,
because an extern thread-local could come from a shared object.  It is
RTEMS that constrains the model, through what its run time loader
implements, so RTEMS is where the flag belongs.  GCC picks local-exec on
its own here.

It was previously carried in every user's config.ini.  Moving it into the
clang option spec removes that workaround.  Verified: dl11-o1.o gets TPREL
relocations, and dl01 through dl12 pass apart from dl06, which fails
identically under GCC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 spec/build/cpukit/optclang.yml | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spec/build/cpukit/optclang.yml b/spec/build/cpukit/optclang.yml
index 178d578f9f..5b8abb94ab 100644
--- a/spec/build/cpukit/optclang.yml
+++ b/spec/build/cpukit/optclang.yml
@@ -26,6 +26,16 @@ actions:
 - set-value: --target=${ARCH}${ARCH_BITS}-unknown-rtems${__RTEMS_MAJOR__}
 - substitute: null
 - env-append: ABI_FLAGS
+# RTEMS uses static thread-local storage.  clang defaults to the initial-exec
+# model for an extern thread-local, which emits R_RISCV_TLS_GOT_HI20 and needs
+# a GOT entry the linker fills in.  That resolves in the base image, but a
+# module loaded by libdl is relocated at run time with no linker involved, and
+# the architecture back ends implement only the local-exec (TPREL) forms -- see
+# rtems_rtl_elf_reloc_rela(), which rejects the TLS GOT relocation.  Ask for
+# local-exec so a loadable module gets relocations libdl can apply.  GCC picks
+# local-exec here on its own.
+- set-value: -ftls-model=local-exec
+- env-append: ABI_FLAGS
 - script: |
     conf.load("ar asm clang clang++ gccdeps")
 
